# GitHub reads this for its "Cite this repository" button. Zenodo reads .zenodo.json
# instead, kept in step by hand (pyproject.toml's [tool.citesync] says why). Software
# indexes read codemeta.json. Edit this file only, then
# run `just citation` to bring codemeta.json in line; the citesync git hook fails while they or the package manifests disagree. Check the name split below:
# the first word becomes the given name.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: "r9lab-vocabulary"
abstract: "A SKOS vocabulary of product types and of component and material classes for repair and disassembly records, with typed crosswalks to CPC 2.1, UNU-KEYs, WEEE categories, PMDco, Wikidata and BAFU activity names, and an SSSOM mapping of the R9lab lab tags with a separate review log."
authors:
  - given-names: "Simon"
    family-names: "van Lierde"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6953-909X"
    email: "code@duinlab.nl"
repository-code: "https://github.com/simonvanlierde/r9lab-vocabulary"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - SKOS
  - controlled vocabulary
  - SSSOM
  - linked data
  - life cycle assessment
  - e-waste
  - repair
  - materials
